{"h":3390,"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.013081394746943587,"x":0.071868583581751869,"w":0.016427103678385416,"c":1,"y":0.50581395368030735,"t":"F"},{"t":"Reading","c":1,"y":0.048179956834590865,"x":0.82493423316192682,"w":0.083254998524983748,"h":0.016288263326549202},{"w":0.80082132975260423,"h":0.016048398200741221,"x":0.10677619332671232,"t":"But environmental and legal groups have urged caution, arguing there are potentially massive","y":0.0958702063303154,"c":1},{"w":0.75564682006835937,"y":0.11327433608349624,"x":0.11704311965539631,"t":"and unknown ramifications for the environment and for nearby communities, and that the","c":1,"h":0.017539617375286642},{"y":0.12854060264985112,"t":"global regulatory framework is not yet drafted. 'Despite arising in the last half century,","c":1,"w":0.73317382812499998,"h":0.019740045598122924,"x":0.11904977076643131},{"t":"the \"new global gold rush\" of deep-sea mining shares many features with past resource","h":0.018979384835842494,"c":1,"x":0.11909651689525314,"w":0.73511291503906251,"y":0.14680232588965836},{"t":"scrambles - including a general disregard for environmental and social impacts, and the","c":1,"w":0.74332646687825521,"x":0.11704313196688322,"y":0.16715116290603693,"h":0.016034677668658737},{"h":0.020908101399739643,"t":"marginalisation of indigenous peoples and their rights,' a paper, written by Julie Hunter","c":1,"y":0.18175917560212729,"w":0.73936035156250002,"x":0.116983619774763},{"w":0.75359344482421875,"t":"and Julian Aguon, from Blue Ocean Law, and Pradeep Singh, from the Center for Marine","x":0.11909650143470514,"c":1,"h":0.017441860412777732,"y":0.20203488374139955},{"t":"Environmental Sciences, Bremen, argues. The authors say that knowledge of the deep seabed","w":0.78644765218098955,"x":0.1190965023310747,"y":0.21946902638849708,"h":0.018903066134382529,"c":1},{"t":"remains extremely limited.ồạiThe surface of the Moon, Mars and even Venus have all been","h":0.020572234747332385,"c":1,"x":0.11697228118129582,"y":0.23618576816289105,"w":0.75784937540690112},{"h":0.017503601681869707,"x":0.11909652054273674,"y":0.25575221224183076,"c":1,"w":0.75975357055664061,"t":"mapped and studied in much greater detail, leading marine scientists to commonly remark"},{"c":1,"t":"that, with respect to the deep sea, \"We don't yet know what we need to know®.?","x":0.11890579973200203,"y":0.26921701324726643,"w":0.66985310872395842,"h":0.025248493205832778},{"t":"Scientific research - including a recent paper in Marine Policy journal - has suggested the","x":0.11498973204669502,"y":0.30959302337092864,"w":0.77207392374674477,"h":0.016070693362075672,"c":1},{"x":0.11699171279335331,"w":0.7434413146972656,"t":"deep seabed, and hydrothermal vents, which are created when seawater meets volcanic","y":0.32552703964510432,"h":0.019809709397037412,"c":1},{"y":0.34302325630530195,"c":1,"x":0.11909652039117087,"t":"magma, have crucial impacts upon biodiversity and the global climate. The mineral-rich","w":0.7515400187174478,"h":0.018923646369866542},{"w":0.78850102742513017,"y":0.36191860445930879,"x":0.11909651385416983,"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"t":"vents and their surrounds are also home to many well-known animals including crustaceans,"},{"h":0.017441860412777732,"w":0.76796712239583342,"c":1,"x":0.11704313282828631,"t":"tubeworms, clams, slugs, anemones and fish. 'It is becoming increasingly clear that deep-","y":0.38081395350980174},{"y":0.39675516223297502,"t":"sea mining poses a grave threat to these vital seabed functions,' the paper says. 'Extraction","x":0.11704312682376222,"w":0.77412729899088539,"h":0.018942511679500229,"c":1},{"w":0.78644765218098966,"x":0.11704311425974452,"c":1,"y":0.41710914440966174,"h":0.016030390354032642,"t":"methods would produce large sediment plumes and involve the discharge of waste back into"},{"c":1,"y":0.4325519208144919,"h":0.01968029326042231,"t":"the ocean, significantly disturbing seafloor environments,' the paper continues. 'On deep","x":0.11699076550863415,"w":0.75574986775716146},{"c":1,"w":0.75988433837890623,"t":"sea vents, scientists are clear;' says Dr Jon Copley of the National Oceanography Centre,","y":0.45057253264214037,"h":0.020384436863361888,"x":0.11698715041179772},{"h":0.017543904689912626,"c":1,"x":0.11909650309822287,"t":"Southampton:iwe don't want mining on them.'","y":0.46947674420594177,"w":0.40862424214680992},{"x":0.11704311116713199,"w":0.68788503011067714,"t":"The oceans occupy around 70% of the planet and are relatively unexplored, says","y":0.50581395360221515,"h":0.016014954896099831,"c":1},{"y":0.52325581397310061,"x":0.11909651435625287,"h":0.017452150530519739,"c":1,"t":"Mike Johnston, chief executive of Nautilus, a Canadian underwater exploration company:","w":0.76591374715169258},{"w":0.75975357055664061,"c":1,"t":"'It makes sense to explore this untapped potential in an environmentally sustainable way,","y":0.5406976744340074,"x":0.11909652082607294,"h":0.017441860412777732},{"t":"instead of continually looking at the fast depleting land resources of the planet to meet","x":0.11704311909774087,"w":0.73921971638997397,"y":0.55958702056786414,"h":0.015994374660615707,"c":1},{"t":"society's rising needs.' Those leading the global rush to place giant mining machines","x":0.11704312501565833,"y":0.5769911504138413,"h":0.01603210527988308,"w":0.72484598795572919,"c":1},{"y":0.59587020642190036,"w":0.71868581136067711,"h":0.014594909645463172,"c":1,"t":"thousands of metres below the sea surface say the environmental impacts will be far","x":0.1170431311862842},{"y":0.61327433617548044,"h":0.016224188790560534,"c":1,"t":"lower than on land. But critics say exotic and little-known ecosystems in the deep","x":0.11704311782667712,"w":0.69815195719401046},{"x":0.11693839914426765,"w":0.755878651936849,"y":0.62867440812292186,"t":"oceans could be destroyed and must be protected. 'Mining will be the greatest assault on","c":1,"h":0.020893377118406109},{"t":"deep-sea ecosystems ever inflicted by humans,' according to hydrothermal vent expert","c":1,"w":0.73716629028320313,"x":0.11704313878036961,"y":0.64680232588965825,"h":0.018979384835842494},{"t":"Verena Tunnicliffe, at the University of Victoria in Canada. She argues that active vents","y":0.66715116281420817,"c":1,"x":0.11909650745588285,"h":0.017509603922345907,"w":0.74743326822916656},{"w":0.75154001871744791,"h":0.017471873303078533,"c":1,"t":"must be off-limits for mining to protect the new knowledge and biotechnology spin-offs","y":0.68459302327924076,"x":0.11704313223400789},{"y":0.70144047529079068,"c":1,"w":0.57715682983398431,"t":"they can deliver, and that strict controls must be in place elsewhere.","h":0.01999611643563326,"x":0.11901364997045324},{"y":0.92441860489760386,"t":"89","w":0.024640657107035335,"h":0.013081394746943587,"x":0.88090349064566109,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51176469618764042,"w":0.45882354736328113,"h":0.04166666666666663,"y":0.94166666658950615}]}